stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Unissued
    Unissued --> Issued: issue_email_otp! / pending parent, candidate and purpose bound
    Issued --> Issued: resend / new generation and keyed verifier
    Issued --> Issued: deliver_email_otp! / locked current generation and authentic code
    Issued --> Consumed: verify_email_otp! / exact bindings and code; admission; fresh clock; single consume
    Unissued --> Cancelled: cancel_email_otp!
    Issued --> Cancelled: cancel_email_otp! / erase verifier
    Issued --> Expired: database deadline reached
    Consumed --> Consumed: email_otp_verified_evidence? / original binding and fixed live receipt; no mutation
    Consumed --> [*]
    Cancelled --> [*]
    Expired --> [*]
    note right of Issued
        Separate email policy on Client, Visitor and Operator ceremony models.
        Stored HMAC binds realm, channel, transaction, purpose, actor,
        session, operation, candidate, destination digest, generation and OTP deadline.
        Wrong binding/code never consumes.
        Transport and verification require finite parent and OTP deadlines.
        APP/COM withdrawal and recovery reentry use this proof and both failure budgets.
        Noticed references bind generation; Mailer rechecks after rendering.
        Other legacy HTTP caller migrations remain incomplete.
    end note
    note right of Consumed
        Challenge verifier is erased; normal verification and transport refuse replay.
        A separate domain-keyed receipt binds original proof and both result timestamps.
        Result deadline is min(verification plus 60 seconds, original transaction expiry).
        SQL timestamp replacement cannot authenticate a longer result window.
    end note
